<title>USA: U.S. Oct non-farm payrolls rose 210,000.</title>
<headline>U.S. Oct non-farm payrolls rose 210,000.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Labor Department</p>
<p>seasonally adjusted jobs data.</p>
<p> In 1,000s--Change	Oct   Sept--(Prev)  Aug--(Prev)  Oct95</p>
<p>  in Nonfarm Payrolls   210    -35    -40    280   241     126</p>
<p> Jobless Rate (Pct)     5.2    5.2    5.2    5.1   5.1     5.5</p>
<p>Earnings, Hours of Private, Non-Farm Production workers:</p>
<p>    -			 Oct  Sept--(Prev)   Aug--(Prev)  Oct95</p>
<p>Earnings/Hour(dollars)  11.91  11.91  11.92  11.87  11.86  11.55</p>
<p> Avg Weekly Hours	34.3   34.7   34.7   34.4   34.5   34.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing Hours   41.6   41.8   41.8   41.7   41.7   41.4</p>
<p> -Overtime Hours	  4.5    4.5    4.5    4.5    4.5    4.3</p>
<p>Non-Farm Month-On-Month Payroll Changes by Industry:</p>
<p>    In 1,000s --	  Oct   Sept--(Prev)  Aug--(Prev)  Oct95</p>
<p> Goods-Producing	   17    -53    -50     34    30     -25</p>
<p> -Construction	     10	8	9     10    11	13</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	     6    -59    -57     24    18     -37</p>
<p> Service-Producing	193     18     10    246   211     151</p>
<p> -Retail		     62     27     22	1     4	 5</p>
<p> -Services		  119     56     54     84    69	83</p>
<p> -Government		-40    -67    -81    122   109	14</p>
<p>Aggregate Weekly Hours Indexes, Seasonally Adj. (1982=100)</p>
<p>    -			  Oct	Sept---(Prev)    Oct95</p>
<p> Total Private	    136.8    138.1    138.0    134.3</p>
<p> -Goods-Producing	 110.2    110.3    110.3    109.6</p>
<p> --Manufacturing	  105.7    106.1    106.1    106.2</p>
<p> -Service-Producing     148.7    150.5    150.5    145.5</p>
<p>Note--The indexes show total aggregate hours of production or nonsupervisory workers on private nonfarm payrolls by industry.  </p>
<p>Number of Workers by Industry, Seasonally Adj. (1,000s):</p>
<p>    -			  Oct	Sept---(Prev)    Oct95</p>
<p> Total Non-Farm	 120,227  120,017  119,990  117,749</p>
<p> Goods-Producing	 24,262   24,245   24,245   24,151</p>
<p> -Construction	    5,455    5,445    5,447    5,200</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	  18,238   18,232   18,229   18,378</p>
<p> --Durable Goods	 10,674   10,676   10,673   10,631</p>
<p> --Non-Durable Goods    7,564    7,556    7,556    7,747</p>
<p>Number of Workers by Industry, Seasonally Adj. (1,000s):</p>
<p>    -			  Oct	Sept---(Prev)    Oct95</p>
<p> Service-Producing     95,965   95,772   95,745   93,598</p>
<p> -Transp./Utilities     6,337    6,330    6,343    6,212</p>
<p> -Wholesale Trade	 6,632    6,613    6,603    6,465</p>
<p> -Retail Trade	   21,761   21,699   21,698   21,263</p>
<p>-Finance, Insurance,</p>
<p>  and Real Estate	 7,029    7,003    7,005    6,859</p>
<p> --Services		34,707   34,588   34,586   33,460</p>
<p> --Help Supply	    2,391    2,402    2,394    2,221</p>
<p> -Government	     19,499   19,539   19,510   19,339</p>
<p>The non-farm payroll data are based on a survey of employers and the jobless rate is based on a survey of households.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected a October rise in non-farm payrolls of 212,000 and a jobless rate of 5.2 percent. They also had forecast a 0.4 percent rise in October average hourly earnings and an average work week of 34.6 hours.  </p>
<p>The household survey also indicated that October employment rose 259,000, that the labor force expanded by 234,000, and the number of unemployed fell 23,000.</p>
